    "id": "10.1038/s41522-026-01201-6",
    "title": "Phages rewire bacterial fitness: beyond killing in host-associated disease",
    "abstract": "Temperate and lytic phages can redirect host-associated bacterial phenotypes through distinct mechanisms. Lytic phages may attenuate virulence when resistance carries pleiotropic costs, whereas prophage-encoded regulation can directly enhance bacterial fitness. We propose that these outcomes represent complementary routes of phage-mediated phenotypic filtering, determined by how phage susceptibility, resistance pathways, or phage-encoded functions intersect with bacterial traits governing colonization, immunity, and disease.",
